WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.630
Following the bombing of Pan Am flight 103
over Scotland, a deal was reached between

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:15.090
Ghadaffi of Libya and the British government
in which the trial of the accused bombers

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:20.520
would happen in a neutral country in return
for the extradition of the accused bombers.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.520
The Netherlands agreed to host the trial,
and so a portion of the Netherlands, a former

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:29.619
NATO base called Camp Zeist, became a piece
of Scottish land in the Netherlands.

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:34.860
This land was part of Scotland, with Scottish
police officers, Scottish judges, and Scottish

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:35.860
law.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.350
Thus the court established on the site for
the proceedings was dubbed the Scottish Court

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:40.910
in the Netherlands.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:45.300
Following the trial and a subsequent appeal,
the land was ceded back to the Netherlands,

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:50.390
but for that short time, Scotland was just
a tiny bit bigger.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:54.690
Across the channel in the area that’s always
Scotland, there are two islands called Westerly

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:56.520
and Papa Westerly.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:00.800
The airports of these two islands can boast
that between them runs the shortest regularly

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.360
scheduled commercial flight in the world.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:09.250
It takes a mere minute, costs 17 pounds, and
travels 1.7 miles (2.7 km)—roughly the same

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:14.390
distance as the runway of the airport of Edinburgh—the
capital of Scotland.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.530
There are a number of places also called Edinburgh
around the world, but the coolest is Edinburgh

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:20.170
of the Seven Seas.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:24.490
Located on the British overseas territory
island of Tristan da Cunha, Edinburgh of the

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:28.890
Seven Seas is considered to be the most remote
inhabited place on earth.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:33.280
The island is 1,200 miles (1,930 km) from
the closest other inhabited place, the island

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:38.430
of St. Helena, and 1,500 miles (2,410 km)from
the nearest continental land, South Africa.

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:44.060
There is no airport and no regular transport
links off of the island.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:48.540
The only way the 300 residents can reach the
rest of the world is by hitching a ride on

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:52.380
a fishing boat, and those only come 8 or 9
times a year.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:57.860
At 64 square miles (103 sq km), Tristin da
Cunha is the 1060th largest island in the

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:03.100
world, but the 8th largest island in the world
is Victoria Island, Canada.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:09.030
On Victoria Island, there's a lake which is
home to an island, which has a lake on it,

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.769
with one more island.

00:02:10.769 --> 00:02:15.520
This tiny four-acre island is so remote that
it is thought that no human has ever set foot

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:16.569
on it.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:20.750
Victoria Island, the island that holds the
lake that holds the island that has that lake

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:24.860
with this island, is slightly bigger than
Great Britain yet has a population of less

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:26.530
than 2,000.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:30.120
Also in Canada, but much farther South is
Vancouver.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:35.180
About 22 miles south of downtown Vancouver
is Point Roberts, Washington, which is part

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:39.910
of the United States, however you cannot get
to the rest of the USA without crossing into

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:41.010
Canada.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:45.670
This is because Point Roberts lies south of
the 49th parallel which constitutes much of

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:48.129
the border between the two countries.

00:02:48.129 --> 00:02:52.220
A few thousand miles to the east, the border
isn’t quite as nice and straight.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:57.440
In Detroit, you counterintuitively have to
travel south to get Canada, America’s northern

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:58.620
neighbor.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:03.640
Also counterintuitively, the westernmost point
of Virginia is actually more westerly than

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.580
the westernmost point of West Virginia.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:10.710
And to finish off the counterintuitivlies,
the eastern end of the Panama Canal flows

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:15.830
into the Pacific Ocean, the ocean to the west,
while the western end of the Panama Canal

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:18.620
flows into the Atlantic Ocean, the ocean to
the east.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:23.250
While we’re so close to South America, I
might as well mention that there are no bridges

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:27.480
over the Amazon River, the second longest
river in the world.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:31.000
This is not because the river is too wide
or anything, but rather because pretty much

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.670
nobody lives around the Amazon.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:37.190
There is actually only one bridge over any
of the major tributaries to the Amazon as

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:38.520
well.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:43.530
For the few roads there are that cross the
Amazon, ferries connect the two sides.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:48.610
And to finish it off let’s head over to
Afghanistan, which has a time zone of UTC

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:50.310
+ 4:30.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:55.010
They’re one of a few nations in the world
that align themselves to a half-hour difference

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:58.150
compared to universal time.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:02.439
Afghanistan shares a brief 47 mile (76 kilometer)
border with China, which has one time zone

00:04:02.439 --> 00:04:04.650
for the entire country.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:10.030
This means that if you step across the Afghanistan-China
border you travel three and a half hours into

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:30.870
the future, and this is the greatest time-zone
change you can make in one step on earth.

